('beginner', 1, 'Strength Foundation', 'Weeks 1-3', 'Build the strength base first — below 1.6x BM, strength is the priority (Turner 2021)', ARRAY['Resistance','Isometric','RFD','Accessory']::text[], '[{"name": "PUSH (Strength)", "rows": [{"num": "1", "exercise": "DB Goblet Squat", "reps": "8", "sets": 3, "velocity": "Controlled", "pct1rm": 0.65, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "120 sec", "method": "Resistance", "yellow_sub": "Drop 1 set", "red_sub": "Wall sit 3 x 30s"}, {"num": "2a", "exercise": "Bench Press / DB Press", "reps": "6", "sets": 3, "velocity": "Controlled", "pct1rm": 0.7, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "120 sec", "method": "Resistance", "yellow_sub": "Reduce to 5 reps", "red_sub": "Iso bench hold 3 x 5s"}, {"num": "2b", "exercise": "Plank -> push-up start", "reps": "5", "sets": 2, "velocity": "Slow", "pct1rm": null, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "60 sec", "method": "Isometric", "yellow_sub": "Keep", "red_sub": "Hold 20s"}, {"num": "3", "exercise": "Step-up", "reps": "6 ea leg", "sets": 2, "velocity": "Fast", "pct1rm": null, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "90 sec", "method": "RFD", "yellow_sub": "Bodyweight", "red_sub": "Split-squat iso 3 x 5s"}, {"num": "4", "exercise": "Med-ball chest pass", "reps": "5", "sets": 2, "velocity": "Fast as possible", "pct1rm": null, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "60 sec", "method": "Plyo", "yellow_sub": "5 reps", "red_sub": "Wall iso push 3 x 5s"}]}, {"name": "PULL (Strength)", "rows": [{"num": "1", "exercise": "Trap-bar / DB Deadlift", "reps": "8", "sets": 3, "velocity": "Controlled", "pct1rm": 0.65, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "120 sec", "method": "Resistance", "yellow_sub": "Drop 1 set", "red_sub": "Glute bridge 3 x 10"}, {"num": "2a", "exercise": "Inverted row / Lat pulldown", "reps": "8", "sets": 3, "velocity": "Controlled", "pct1rm": null, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "90 sec", "method": "Resistance", "yellow_sub": "Keep", "red_sub": "Band row 3 x 10"}, {"num": "2b", "exercise": "Hip hinge (dowel)", "reps": "8", "sets": 2, "velocity": "Controlled", "pct1rm": null, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "60 sec", "method": "Accessory", "yellow_sub": "Keep", "red_sub": "Keep"}, {"num": "3", "exercise": "DB RDL", "reps": "8", "sets": 2, "velocity": "Controlled", "pct1rm": 0.55, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "90 sec", "method": "Resistance", "yellow_sub": "Keep", "red_sub": "Reduce load"}, {"num": "4", "exercise": "Med-ball slam", "reps": "5", "sets": 2, "velocity": "Fast", "pct1rm": null, "dropoff": null, "cluster_rest": "—", "set_rest": "60 sec", "method": "Plyo", "yellow_sub": "5 reps", "red_sub": "Skip"}]}]'::jsonb, 'fv_power_12w', 'Force-Velocity Power (12-week)', 'explosive_power', 'athletic_explosive_power', '12-week power programme periodized across the force-velocity curve: Strength Foundation -> Strength-Speed -> Speed-Strength/Optimal Load -> Speed/Peaking. Strength is the vehicle for power (Haff & Nimphius 2012); velocity targets + <=20% velocity-loss caps (Weakley 2021); pulling derivatives above the knee (Turner 2021).', 3, '[{"year": 2021, "citation": "Weakley, Mann, Banyard, McLaren, Scott, Garcia-Ramos (2021). Velocity-Based Training: From Theory to Application", "journal": "Strength & Conditioning Journal 43(2):31-49", "focus": "Use velocity to prescribe and autoregulate load. Velocity-loss thresholds end the set: ~10% VL = least fatigue/highest quality, 20% VL = balance, 30%+ = more volume/hypertrophy. Minimum-velocity thresholds (V1RM) per lift; 2-point load-velocity profile (~45% & ~85% 1RM) estimates 1RM."}, {"year": 2012, "citation": "Haff & Nimphius (2012). Training Principles for Power", "journal": "Strength & Conditioning Journal 34(6):2-12", "focus": "Maximal strength is the foundation of power. Optimal load maximizes power output; a mixed-methods approach (heavy + optimal-load + ballistic across the F-V spectrum) develops power best. ~2x bodyweight squat is the benchmark for specialized power work."}, {"year": 2021, "citation": "Turner, Comfort, McMahon, Bishop, Chavda, Read, Mundy, Lake (2021). Developing Powerful Athletes Part 1 & 2", "journal": "Strength & Conditioning Journal 43(1):23-31 & 43(2)", "focus": "Most sport actions occur in <0.3 s, so RFD/impulse matters. Velocity zones (back squat MCV): Strength 0.23-0.5, Strength-Speed >0.5-1.0, Speed-Strength 1.0-1.5, Speed >1.5 m/s. Force-deficit athletes emphasize ballistic; velocity-deficit emphasize strength; swap each mesocycle. Weightlifting pulls above the knee suit novices (full triple extension, no catch)."}]'::jsonb),
